              They are not committed to this repository.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. ONNX Runtime (transitive dependency via fastembed)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Project:   https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime
   License:   MIT License
   Role:      ONNX model inference runtime

================================================================================
Upstream public data
================================================================================

Ingested corpus records (literature, trial registries, priors, and similar) are
sourced from third-party public databases. Each source remains subject to its
provider's terms of use. This repository does not ship the full built corpus in
git; see `docs/engine.md` for how to build or obtain `vitiligo.db`.

Sources read by the engine, with the terms they are served under. Where a
licence requires attribution, serving data derived from that source carries the
attribution with it:

   Open Targets Platform      CC0 1.0 (data); Apache-2.0 (their code).
                              https://platform-docs.opentargets.org/licence
                              Upstream sources within the Platform keep their
                              own licences; the Platform lists them per source.

   ChEMBL                     Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0
                              Unported. Attribution is required, and
                              adaptations carry the same licence.
                              https://chembl.gitbook.io/chembl-interface-documentation/about

   PubMed / PMC               NLM terms; per-article copyright and licence vary,
                              and PMC Open Access subsets carry their own.
                              https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/home/about/policies/

   GEO                        NCBI terms, as above.

   ClinicalTrials.gov         https://clinicaltrials.gov/about-site/terms-conditions
   EU CTR (CTIS)              https://euclinicaltrials.eu
   WHO ICTRP                  https://www.who.int/clinical-trials-registry-platform
   ISRCTN                     https://www.isrctn.com

   GWAS Catalog               EMBL-EBI terms.
                              https://www.ebi.ac.uk/gwas/docs/about
   NIH RePORTER               https://reporter.nih.gov

Licence names above were checked for Open Targets and ChEMBL; the remaining
entries link to the provider's terms rather than restate them. An operator
serving this engine publicly is responsible for complying with each.

The web application filters cross-references and provenance naming a source
whose terms do not permit redistribution (currently DrugBank) out of its
responses, so what it serves does not depend on which optional sources the
operator has imported.

DrugBank support is import-only. This repository does not bundle DrugBank
database content, API results, or derived DrugBank datasets. Parser tests use a
synthetic DrugBank-shaped XML fixture. Users who enable DrugBank ingestion must
bring their own appropriately licensed export and comply with DrugBank's
redistribution and citation terms.

================================================================================
Optional cloud API (not bundled)
================================================================================

The `vitiligo ask` and `vitiligo hypothesize` commands call the Anthropic
Messages API when `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is configured. They are command-line
tools: the web application serves no generated content and makes no call to
any model API. That service is not part of this distribution; use is governed
by Anthropic's terms at https://www.anthropic.com/legal.
